# Powered Up over Web Bluetooth

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # Until ex_lwp is on Hex. Then use {:ex_lwp, "~> 0.1.0"}
  {:ex_lwp, github: "ErikMejerHansen/ex_lwp"},
  {:kino_web_bluetooth, "~> 0.1.0"}
])
```

## About

This notebook talks to a LEGO® Powered Up hub (City Hub, Technic Hub,
Boost Move Hub, ...) from Livebook.
[KinoWebBluetooth](https://github.com/ErikMejerHansen/kino_web_bluetooth)
carries the bytes over your browser's Web Bluetooth, and
[ExLWP](https://github.com/ErikMejerHansen/ex_lwp) turns them into LEGO
Wireless Protocol messages.

You need a Chromium based browser (Chrome, Edge). Press the hub's button
so it advertises (its light blinks).

> ExLWP and KinoWebBluetooth are not affiliated with, sponsored,
> authorized or endorsed by The LEGO Group. LEGO® and Powered Up are
> trademarks of The LEGO Group.

## Connect

Evaluate the Smart Cell below, click **Connect** and pick your hub. The
service UUID is already set to the LEGO Hub Service.

